<article class="env-lemma" id="0C28">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C28">Lemma <span data-tag="0C28">15.110.1</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The map $A^ h \to A^\wedge $ defines a surjective map from minimal primes of $A^\wedge $ to minimal primes of $A^ h$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The number of branches of $A$ is at most the number of branches of $A^\wedge $. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The number of geometric branches of $A$ is at most the number of geometric branches of $A^\wedge $. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/06LJ" data-tag="06LJ">15.46.3</a> the map $A^ h \to A^\wedge $ is flat and injective. Combining going down (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HS" data-tag="00HS">10.39.19</a>) and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00FK" data-tag="00FK">10.30.5</a> we see that part (1) holds. Part (2) follows from this, Definition <a href="/tag/0C26" data-tag="0C26">15.108.6</a>, and the fact that $A^\wedge $ is henselian (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04GM" data-tag="04GM">10.153.9</a>). By Lemma <a href="/tag/06LJ" data-tag="06LJ">15.46.3</a> we have $(A^\wedge )^{sh} = A^{sh} \otimes _{A^ h} A^\wedge $. Thus we can repeat the arguments above using the flat injective map $A^{sh} \to (A^\wedge )^{sh}$ to prove (3). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>